  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.usp.ai/Ontologies/FPEO/PowerModule.rdf#PowerDemand">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/Core/InformationContentEntity"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Suggested Reuse
Close to demand/profile modeling in SAREF4ENER.

Rationale: PowerDemand is directly related to:
a specific demand profile;
The BUS demand period datatype property.
That means PowerDemand is best treated as an information artifact specifying required electrical demand, not as a material entity or process.

Formal Definition (DL)

	power:PowerDemand ⊑BFO:GenericallyDependentContinuant
power:PowerDemand ⊑∃ power:hasPowerDemandProfile.power:PowerDemandProfile
power:PowerDemand ⊑∃ power:dependsOnDemandPeriod.power:BUS

Elucidation
A PowerDemand is a specified electrical-demand requirement associated with a BUS and constrained by the BUS demand period. It is interpreted through a demand profile that provides the defining curve or formula.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>FPEO - power:PowerDemand [002-001]</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
